# ---- Analytics database (omnischools-analytics-prod) ----
# Oversight reads ONLY this DB. Locally, a second Docker Postgres or a Supabase branch.
# The app should connect as a NON-OWNER, read-scoped role so RLS applies (see db/sql/policies.sql).
ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://omnischools:omnischools@localhost:55432/omnischools_analytics_dev"

# ---- Gated named-record read-back to OPERATIONAL Postgres (OVERSIGHT_ANALYTICS_SPEC §6) ----
# Separate, scoped, logged connection used ONLY by the compliance record surface. Leave blank
# until that surface is wired. Never point the whole app at operational data.
#
# MUST be a dedicated read-only role on the OPERATIONAL project with an explicit per-table SELECT
# allow-list (staff_profile, ref_role, role_assignment, facilities_snapshot,
# school_staff_oversight_consent — and nothing else, notably NOT staff_compensation), no write/DDL,
# and a statement_timeout. Full posture + the exact GRANTs: docs/PROVISIONING.md §4a.
#
# UNSET = FAIL CLOSED. With this blank, the individual drill-down surface must refuse (aggregates
# only). Never fall back to ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL for it.
OPERATIONAL_READBACK_URL=

# ---- Supabase (analytics project — GES staff auth, NOT the school-auth project) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---- Public site URL (metadata; oversight.omnischools.gh in prod) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3100

# ---- Observability (dormant unless set) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# ---- Dev auth shim ----
# true = ADMIN dev session (local dev). false + Supabase env = real GES-staff auth. FAIL CLOSED.
#
# ⚠ The shim returns a NATIONAL officer — the tier with NO jurisdiction filter — without
# authenticating anyone. In production that is unauthenticated national access to every named
# record, logged against a fabricated officer id. So the app REFUSES TO START when this is true and
# NODE_ENV=production (lib/auth/index.ts): a misconfigured deploy fails loudly at boot instead of
# quietly opening the door. Keep it true locally; it must be false on every deployed environment.
AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=true

# ---- E3 feature flag: individual drill-down of non-GES staff at NON-PUBLIC schools ----
# DEFAULT false, and it MUST stay false in production until a DPO writes the lawful-basis position
# for private/mission-school staff under the Data Protection Act 2012 (Act 843) — an employer's
# click is not the employee's consent (apps/web/Todo.md "Blocked on").
#
# false = a school whose ownership_type is PRIVATE or MISSION is refused the OTHER_STAFF individual
#         drill-down BEFORE any operational fetch, even if that school has recorded DPO consent.
#         The refusal is a logged DENIED_NO_CONSENT audit row, not a silent no-op.
# GES-establishment teachers are STATUTORY at every ownership type and never consult this flag.
E3_NON_PUBLIC_STAFF_DRILLDOWN=false
